    "tiptap_body": {
      "body": {
        "type": "doc",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "paragraph",
            "content": [
              {
                "text": "One thing I’ve been excited about is the chance I have to get my department ",
                "type": "text",
                "circle_ios_fallback_text": "One thing I’ve been excited about is the chance I have to get my department "
              },
              {
                "text": "dialed in",
                "type": "text",
                "marks": [
                  {
                    "type": "italic"
                  }
                ],
                "circle_ios_fallback_text": "dialed in"
              },
              {
                "text": " with this operating system we’ve building. I like to refer to my department as the “R&D department” of the college as we are entirely non-credit workforce training focused. Without having to navigate a massive amount of red tape from the federal, state, and even institutional governing bodies, I can operate in the “wild west” and try things very easily. ",
                "type": "text",
                "circle_ios_fallback_text": " with this operating system we’ve building. I like to refer to my department as the “R&D department” of the college as we are entirely non-credit workforce training focused. Without having to navigate a massive amount of red tape from the federal, state, and even institutional governing bodies, I can operate in the “wild west” and try things very easily. "
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "type": "paragraph",
            "content": [
              {
                "text": "I have found it helpful to focus my efforts on my biggest and best run program (CDL-License training) so I can spend more time understanding the EMPOWER system and less on trying to fix a struggling program. I’m already excited to apply this to all my other training programs after the cohort finishes, and then to my department as a whole. Once I do that, I want to show it to my boss and see if i can get buy in to help roll this out at a divisional level. I see a lot of opportunity to help my very process-bloated institution to improve!",
                "type": "text",
                "circle_ios_fallback_text": "I have found it helpful to focus my efforts on my biggest and best run program (CDL-License training) so I can spend more time understanding the EMPOWER system and less on trying to fix a struggling program. I’m already excited to apply this to all my other training programs after the cohort finishes, and then to my department as a whole. Once I do that, I want to show it to my boss and see if i can get buy in to help roll this out at a divisional level. I see a lot of opportunity to help my very process-bloated institution to improve!"
              }
            ]
          }
        ]
      },
      "circle_ios_fallback_text": "One thing I’ve been excited about is the chance I have to get my department dialed in with this operating system we’ve building. I like to refer to my department as the “R&D department” of the college as we are entirely non-credit workforce training focused. Without having to navigate a massive amount of red tape from the federal, state, and even institutional governing bodies, I can operate in the “wild west” and try things very easily. I have found it helpful to focus my efforts on my biggest and best run program (CDL-License training) so I can spend more time understanding the EMPOWER system and less on trying to fix a struggling program. I’m already excited to apply this to all my other training programs after the cohort finishes, and then to my department as a whole. Once I do that, I want to show it to my boss and see if i can get buy in to help roll this out at a divisional level. I see a lot of opportunity to help my very process-bloated institution to improve!",
