    "tiptap_body": {
      "body": {
        "type": "doc",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "paragraph",
            "content": [
              {
                "text": "It's taken me quite a bit of time to work through all the Session 5 homework. Part of the difficulty with this is that our college has a marketing team that has its own metrics and software. I may put in a request to the marketing team, and we can start a campaign or do some targeted advertising, but I'm not in charge of any of that directly.",
                "type": "text",
                "circle_ios_fallback_text": "It's taken me quite a bit of time to work through all the Session 5 homework. Part of the difficulty with this is that our college has a marketing team that has its own metrics and software. I may put in a request to the marketing team, and we can start a campaign or do some targeted advertising, but I'm not in charge of any of that directly."
              },
              {
                "type": "hardBreak",
                "circle_ios_fallback_text": "\n"
              },
              {
                "type": "hardBreak",
                "circle_ios_fallback_text": "\n"
              },
              {
                "text": "As I was going through this with Claude, I tried to be very clear on my situation. About halfway through, it got a good enough grasp of what I'm doing that it asked me if I would like to pivot the entire assignment instead of proceeding with something that wasn’t aligned to me. I did ask it to finish the assignment as originally written so I can get the experience of this class the way it was intended. But I did go down an hour-long rabbit hole with it later as it customized this for me.",
                "type": "text",
                "circle_ios_fallback_text": "As I was going through this with Claude, I tried to be very clear on my situation. About halfway through, it got a good enough grasp of what I'm doing that it asked me if I would like to pivot the entire assignment instead of proceeding with something that wasn’t aligned to me. I did ask it to finish the assignment as originally written so I can get the experience of this class the way it was intended. But I did go down an hour-long rabbit hole with it later as it customized this for me."
              },
              {
                "type": "hardBreak",
                "circle_ios_fallback_text": "\n"
              },
              {
                "type": "hardBreak",
                "circle_ios_fallback_text": "\n"
              },
              {
                "text": "Actually going through these processes help me see how versatile AI can be with different situations. Even though these prompts and these lessons are built to be (roughly) one-size-fits-all for C-suite and company owners, Claude has almost effortlessly made pivots every step of the way. To benefit me and my specific limitations and opportunities.",
                "type": "text",
                "circle_ios_fallback_text": "Actually going through these processes help me see how versatile AI can be with different situations. Even though these prompts and these lessons are built to be (roughly) one-size-fits-all for C-suite and company owners, Claude has almost effortlessly made pivots every step of the way. To benefit me and my specific limitations and opportunities."
              }
            ]
          }
        ]
      },
      "circle_ios_fallback_text": "It's taken me quite a bit of time to work through all the Session 5 homework. Part of the difficulty with this is that our college has a marketing team that has its own metrics and software. I may put in a request to the marketing team, and we can start a campaign or do some targeted advertising, but I'm not in charge of any of that directly.\n\nAs I was going through this with Claude, I tried to be very clear on my situation. About halfway through, it got a good enough grasp of what I'm doing that it asked me if I would like to pivot the entire assignment instead of proceeding with something that wasn’t aligned to me. I did ask it to finish the assignment as originally written so I can get the experience of this class the way it was intended. But I did go down an hour-long rabbit hole with it later as it customized this for me.\n\nActually going through these processes help me see how versatile AI can be with different situations. Even though these prompts and these lessons are built to be (roughly) one-size-fits-all for C-suite and company owners, Claude has almost effortlessly made pivots every step of the way. To benefit me and my specific limitations and opportunities.",
